Package: tsfm
Title: Native Time-Series Foundation Models for R
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Pedro", "Botz", , "pedrobtz@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Zero-shot (and later fine-tuned) forecasting with open
    time-series foundation models, natively in R. Provides a
    'from_pretrained()'-style loader with an architecture registry, native
    'torch' implementations of a curated model catalogue, a shared
    preprocessing contract, explicit capability metadata, batched panel
    inference, and a standard forecast object. Designed tidymodels-first:
    'hardhat'-based formula, data frame, and recipe interfaces, a 'parsnip'
    model specification so models drop into 'workflows', 'tune', and
    'rsample' unchanged, and 'yardstick'-compatible output, with thin
    secondary adapters into the tidyverts and 'modeltime' ecosystems.
